@startuml
title Futurelock deadlock sequence from RFD 0609

participant "Background task" as BG
participant "Main task" as MT
participant "tokio::select!" as SEL
participant "future1\n(op1)" as F1
participant "future2\n(sleep 500ms)" as F2
participant "future3\n(op2)" as F3
participant "Mutex" as M

BG -> M: lock()
M --> BG: acquired
BG -> BG: sleep(5s)

MT -> SEL: enter select!
SEL -> F1: poll
F1 -> M: lock()
M --> F1: queued\nPending

SEL -> F2: poll
F2 --> SEL: Pending

== 500ms later ==

F2 --> MT: wake main task
MT -> SEL: poll branches again
SEL -> F1: poll
F1 --> SEL: still Pending
SEL -> F2: poll
F2 --> SEL: Ready

SEL --> MT: choose sleep branch
note over SEL,F1
The branch using &mut future1 ends,
but future1 itself is not dropped.
end note

MT -> F3: start op2
F3 -> M: lock()
M --> F3: queued behind future1\nPending

== ~4.5s later ==

BG -> M: unlock()
M --> F1: grant lock (fair/FIFO)
M --> MT: wake task responsible for future1

note over MT,F3
Main task is no longer polling future1;
it is only awaiting future3.
end note

F3 --> MT: still Pending\n(waiting for mutex)

note over F1,M
future1 now owns the mutex
but never runs again.
end note

note over MT,M
Deadlock / futurelock:
future3 waits on a mutex held by future1,
and future1 waits for the main task to poll it (never happens).
end note

@enduml
